{"id": "live-362", "title": "NFI Apartment Management, L.L.C. v. Third Coast Insurance Company (Fifth Circuit Affirms Time-Barred Hail Coverage Claim)", "category": "premises-liability", "status": "ruling", "date": "2026-10-20", "jurisdiction": "U.S. Court of Appeals for the Fifth Circuit (W.D. Tex.)", "state": "TX", "amount": "$359,856.60 policy deductible; insurer's damage estimates of roughly $37,058 and later $61,840 both fell below it", "source": "live", "source_url": "https://www.ca5.uscourts.gov/opinions/unpub/25/25-50953.0.pdf", "summary": "The Fifth Circuit affirmed summary judgment for Third Coast Insurance Company against NFI Apartment Management, L.L.C. over a May 2020 hailstorm claim on a San Antonio apartment complex, holding NFI's 2024 breach-of-contract and Texas Insurance Code suit was barred by the policy's contractual limitations period and Texas's statutory limitations periods. Third Coast had found covered damage of about $37,058.29 in a July 21, 2020 letter, below the policy's $359,856.60 deductible, and a later joint reinspection raised that estimate only to about $61,839.72 before Third Coast closed the file in July 2021 -- with the court holding the claim accrued no later than the 2020 denial letter, years before NFI sued.", "significance": "The case is a clean illustration of a recurring trap in first-party commercial property claims: when an insurer's determination is a below-deductible estimate rather than an outright denial, there is no formal 'claim denied' letter to anchor a policyholder's calendar, but courts will still treat that determination as the limitations trigger. Multifamily and other commercial property owners who let a below-deductible estimate or a closed claim file sit for years while continuing informal discussions with an adjuster risk losing their coverage claim entirely before a court ever reaches the merits of whether the damage estimate itself was fair.", "judge": null, "tags": ["insurance coverage", "hail damage", "multifamily", "limitations period", "fifth circuit"]}
